1
00:00:00,772 --> 00:00:09,077
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the pressure of restraint can sometimes make the mind irrational.

2
00:00:09,457 --> 00:00:18,262
[SPEAKER_00]: So, do you have any advice for how to maintain perspective in the face of the irrational mind?

3
00:00:20,663 --> 00:00:29,448
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, maintaining perspective, it's gonna require you losing perspective, so to speak.

4
00:00:30,243 --> 00:00:32,325
[SPEAKER_01]: Maintaining perspective means developing perspective.

5
00:00:33,866 --> 00:00:41,392
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can... you can know what the perspective is, but when the irrational mind is pressuring you, you're going to lose it.

6
00:00:42,453 --> 00:00:45,776
[SPEAKER_01]: Because otherwise, you wouldn't be pressured, or not as pressured.

7
00:00:46,417 --> 00:00:58,587
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why it does boil down to then not acting out of the irrational mind, and feeling that grain that's trying to pull you with... to go with it, and trying to then

8
00:01:01,215 --> 00:01:03,296
[SPEAKER_01]: Exert the right perspective within it.

9
00:01:05,237 --> 00:01:09,278
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not like, oh, I need to get the right perspective for this to go away.

10
00:01:09,898 --> 00:01:11,959
[SPEAKER_01]: More like, no, no, no, this won't be going away.

11
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:18,122
[SPEAKER_01]: The only thing I can and should be doing is have the perspective present with it.

12
00:01:18,862 --> 00:01:20,303
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how it eventually goes away.

13
00:01:21,543 --> 00:01:25,425
[SPEAKER_01]: So, really... and that's not terribly hard to do.

14
00:01:26,465 --> 00:01:28,566
[SPEAKER_01]: What's kind of hard to not forget is to

15
00:01:29,370 --> 00:01:32,532
[SPEAKER_01]: You fall back into the expectation for this pain to go away.

16
00:01:34,012 --> 00:01:44,278
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, whether you're doing a perspective or this, or not acting out as well, you're doing it all under this intention of... so that it goes away.

17
00:01:45,118 --> 00:01:46,199
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why it's not going away.

18
00:01:47,059 --> 00:01:49,140
[SPEAKER_01]: It won't go away because of that very reason.

19
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:49,620
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's like...

20
00:01:50,381 --> 00:01:53,462
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's then more practically...

21
00:01:54,363 --> 00:01:55,964
[SPEAKER_01]: It's better, from a practical point of view,

22
00:01:56,782 --> 00:01:57,102
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no, no.

23
00:01:57,242 --> 00:01:58,584
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not about it going away.

24
00:01:58,804 --> 00:01:59,985
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't want it to go away.

25
00:02:00,686 --> 00:02:07,111
[SPEAKER_01]: I want it to stay here, so that I can present it with a perspective, and then keep it there for as long as it's there.

26
00:02:09,253 --> 00:02:11,535
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like as we said before, like a screaming child.

27
00:02:12,416 --> 00:02:16,440
[SPEAKER_01]: You can do this or that to appease it, so it stops screaming, or you could just

28
00:02:17,949 --> 00:02:19,210
[SPEAKER_01]: Repeat how things are.

29
00:02:19,390 --> 00:02:22,071
[SPEAKER_01]: The actual tell it that, no, this is how it is.

30
00:02:22,511 --> 00:02:23,672
[SPEAKER_01]: And it refuses to hear that.

31
00:02:23,772 --> 00:02:24,692
[SPEAKER_01]: It continues to scream.

32
00:02:25,153 --> 00:02:28,114
[SPEAKER_01]: And you just hold the picture in front of it until it calms down and accepts it.

33
00:02:33,157 --> 00:02:35,117
[SPEAKER_00]: Or the knocking at the door.

34
00:02:36,098 --> 00:02:36,978
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, exactly.

35
00:02:37,539 --> 00:02:39,780
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, but hold on, why am I bothered?

36
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:42,201
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I'm bothered because I do still

37
00:02:43,128 --> 00:02:50,153
[SPEAKER_01]: I carry an assumption that it shouldn't be happening and it shouldn't be anybody in front of my door because it would be better if it's not.

38
00:02:51,254 --> 00:02:52,995
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I want it to not be in front of my door.

39
00:02:53,015 --> 00:02:54,316
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, yeah, but that's not up to you.

40
00:02:55,917 --> 00:03:05,304
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the only reason you're resisting or you're still pressured by somebody in front of your door is because you still carry expectation that I want to go away from in front of my door.

41
00:03:05,444 --> 00:03:07,185
[SPEAKER_01]: I want front of my door to be free and open.

42
00:03:08,186 --> 00:03:09,747
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, but that's not your domain.

43
00:03:14,122 --> 00:03:35,419
[SPEAKER_00]: What if... so... because you start from this position of ignorance and you're just like... sometimes you're even like not aware maybe that you are like subtly, I don't know, opening the door somehow without... Well...

44
00:03:38,907 --> 00:03:40,969
[SPEAKER_01]: There's no reason to mystify it like that.

45
00:03:41,310 --> 00:03:41,890
[SPEAKER_01]: There's always.

46
00:03:42,651 --> 00:03:45,453
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if it's true to some extent, it's irrelevant, really.

47
00:03:45,514 --> 00:03:47,555
[SPEAKER_01]: What's relevant is the stuff that you are aware of.

48
00:03:48,576 --> 00:03:56,003
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, then later on you might find, oh, there are those other subtle ways, but to assume the subtle ways now are responsible for this, they're not.

49
00:03:56,644 --> 00:03:57,044
[SPEAKER_01]: They're not.

50
00:03:57,164 --> 00:03:58,045
[SPEAKER_01]: It's what you're doing now.

51
00:03:58,766 --> 00:04:01,128
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you now still carrying

52
00:04:01,653 --> 00:04:02,754
[SPEAKER_01]: The heavy assembly.

53
00:04:03,054 --> 00:04:05,415
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I refuse to live under this.

54
00:04:05,515 --> 00:04:07,477
[SPEAKER_01]: I want it to go away from the front of my door.

55
00:04:07,577 --> 00:04:08,757
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't want it to be there.

56
00:04:09,698 --> 00:04:10,699
[SPEAKER_01]: That's really the problem.

57
00:04:17,102 --> 00:04:31,051
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's the whole training that boils down to maintaining the perspective, or presenting the perspective, or reminding yourself of the right perspective, in face of that pain that has arisen on account of that irrational pressure.

58
00:04:33,355 --> 00:04:37,498
[SPEAKER_03]: Could you say that you'd be holding up that picture to the child?

59
00:04:39,059 --> 00:04:40,580
[SPEAKER_03]: But, you know, it's not for the child.

60
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:46,403
[SPEAKER_03]: You know, the child could scream forever, but it's for you to remember as well.

61
00:04:47,604 --> 00:04:52,387
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, it's for you to remember for sure, but fundamentally it's so that the child eventually learns.

62
00:04:52,607 --> 00:04:53,608
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

63
00:04:53,628 --> 00:04:55,869
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you can't help but want pain to go away.

64
00:04:56,069 --> 00:04:56,309
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

65
00:04:56,970 --> 00:04:58,931
[SPEAKER_01]: But you can certainly make sure that it's not

66
00:04:59,625 --> 00:05:02,927
[SPEAKER_01]: the root of your immediate intention, like, but I want it now.

67
00:05:02,967 --> 00:05:03,968
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever I do, I want.

68
00:05:04,008 --> 00:05:06,389
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, yeah, you practice because you want to be free from suffering.

69
00:05:06,509 --> 00:05:06,629
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

70
00:05:07,190 --> 00:05:18,737
[SPEAKER_01]: But not in that sense of through that denial, but through the sense of, no, no, I will be free from suffering when the mind stops or loses the ability to become irrational and turn against me and itself.

71
00:05:32,202 --> 00:05:52,305
[SPEAKER_01]: But you could say... you could, like... if you practice this for a while, so you're not acting out, and then pressure comes and goes, sometimes more, sometimes less, sometimes better, sometimes worse, but overall, you're not sliding back in terms of your unwholesome actions, you're not going against the precepts, you're not losing sense restraint.

72
00:05:53,726 --> 00:06:01,367
[SPEAKER_01]: As I said, sometimes you more accurately re-establish perspective, sometimes that's just feel like too much work and you're just weathering it until it stops.

73
00:06:03,868 --> 00:06:05,429
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to go through some extent of that.

74
00:06:05,950 --> 00:06:06,590
[SPEAKER_01]: It's inevitable.

75
00:06:07,551 --> 00:06:17,818
[SPEAKER_01]: But as you're doing it, as I said, even if you're just not acting out, but even if you don't have any perspective at the time, it's still obviously a form of staying with it.

76
00:06:17,858 --> 00:06:19,299
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not like, oh, this is wrong now.

77
00:06:19,379 --> 00:06:19,500
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

78
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:21,921
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no wrong for as long as you don't act out of it.

79
00:06:22,642 --> 00:06:26,805
[SPEAKER_01]: As long as the door is not open, there is nothing wrong what you do inside.

80
00:06:27,622 --> 00:06:32,724
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, it's not the best thing you should do, but it's nowhere near the threshold of it's wrong.

81
00:06:33,805 --> 00:06:36,066
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that's another trick to get you to open the door.

82
00:06:36,466 --> 00:06:37,247
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, it's wrong.

83
00:06:37,287 --> 00:06:38,507
[SPEAKER_01]: I might as well open the door now.

84
00:06:40,368 --> 00:06:43,610
[SPEAKER_01]: But for as long as the door is not open, it's not wrong.

85
00:06:43,710 --> 00:06:44,110
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not wrong.

86
00:06:44,190 --> 00:06:44,970
[SPEAKER_01]: It simply isn't.

87
00:06:45,130 --> 00:06:45,611
[SPEAKER_01]: It cannot be.

88
00:06:46,131 --> 00:06:46,851
[SPEAKER_00]: No matter how much...

89
00:06:46,931 --> 00:06:51,673
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter how confused, how doubtful, how everything else you might be feeling.

90
00:06:51,753 --> 00:06:53,054
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, yeah, but the door's not open.

91
00:06:54,735 --> 00:06:55,015
[SPEAKER_01]: So...

92
00:06:55,452 --> 00:06:56,873
[SPEAKER_01]: It's still better than being open.

93
00:06:57,374 --> 00:07:04,219
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's still more right than it would have been otherwise.

94
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:15,508
[SPEAKER_03]: Is... is that the clarity about what that doorway is always available?

95
00:07:16,489 --> 00:07:19,111
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, whenever there is a pressure, there's a doorway.

96
00:07:21,212 --> 00:07:24,415
[SPEAKER_03]: Like the... the line of... because you can...

97
00:07:25,129 --> 00:07:26,070
[SPEAKER_03]: You lose sight of that.

98
00:07:26,510 --> 00:07:27,831
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, right, yeah.

99
00:07:29,192 --> 00:07:31,453
[SPEAKER_01]: But... Yeah, so...

100
00:07:31,473 --> 00:07:32,614
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the recollection of that.

101
00:07:32,854 --> 00:07:33,235
[SPEAKER_01]: It's...

102
00:07:33,255 --> 00:07:37,618
[SPEAKER_01]: I think, let's say, the doorway is basically if you... if you, like, really act out of it.

103
00:07:39,979 --> 00:07:45,944
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you could be walking towards the door, be on the other side of the door, but not open it.

104
00:07:47,084 --> 00:07:53,309
[SPEAKER_01]: Obviously, if you are constantly just sitting on the other side of the door next to the door handle, well, the pressure to open it will increase.

105
00:07:54,639 --> 00:07:55,980
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you need to recognize that as well.

106
00:07:56,360 --> 00:08:00,903
[SPEAKER_01]: But, fundamentally, as long as you don't open it, you are safe, even if it doesn't feel like that.

107
00:08:05,826 --> 00:08:08,788
[SPEAKER_01]: And it won't feel like that, because that's the only true safety.

108
00:08:10,189 --> 00:08:11,430
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what the Mahārāja presented as.

109
00:08:11,470 --> 00:08:11,810
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no, no.

110
00:08:11,830 --> 00:08:12,991
[SPEAKER_01]: This is the worst thing you can do.

111
00:08:13,011 --> 00:08:13,551
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't do this.

112
00:08:18,874 --> 00:08:19,335
[SPEAKER_01]: But you could.

113
00:08:19,355 --> 00:08:20,595
[SPEAKER_01]: That's... and that's on that part.

114
00:08:20,615 --> 00:08:21,456
[SPEAKER_01]: When you're on the inside,

115
00:08:22,888 --> 00:08:33,572
[SPEAKER_01]: Of the house, when you're not opening the door, but you are kind of getting, like, walking past the door, examining the door, thinking about opening the door, trying to all this.

116
00:08:33,852 --> 00:08:35,933
[SPEAKER_01]: You realize, okay, I could stop that now.

117
00:08:36,833 --> 00:08:42,475
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's that part we talked about before, of, like, not allowing images to take the center stage.

118
00:08:43,795 --> 00:08:51,658
[SPEAKER_01]: And as we said also, I think, in one of the talks, it's like, even without them being the center stage, you already know what they are.

119
00:08:53,287 --> 00:09:00,153
[SPEAKER_01]: So, even if I don't explicitly start thinking about things I'm being pressured and all this and that, if I were to allow it, I know exactly what I will think.

120
00:09:01,214 --> 00:09:01,815
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's like...

121
00:09:01,835 --> 00:09:02,435
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I won't.

122
00:09:02,816 --> 00:09:04,057
[SPEAKER_01]: I won't allow it in the center stage.

123
00:09:04,077 --> 00:09:06,519
[SPEAKER_01]: Again, I'm not trying to get rid of who is in front of the door.

124
00:09:06,999 --> 00:09:12,124
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm not trying to get rid of all these thoughts that are... that would be associated with it.

125
00:09:12,685 --> 00:09:14,486
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm just keeping them into that blur.

126
00:09:14,947 --> 00:09:18,450
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm not allowing them to crystallize through my own efforts.

127
00:09:20,355 --> 00:09:21,855
[SPEAKER_01]: If they pop up on their own, that's fine.

128
00:09:22,315 --> 00:09:26,757
[SPEAKER_01]: That's a completely different thing than if they pop up because I intended them to do so.

129
00:09:27,617 --> 00:09:28,517
[SPEAKER_01]: Although it feels the same.

130
00:09:28,557 --> 00:09:29,817
[SPEAKER_01]: The end result feels the same.

131
00:09:30,157 --> 00:09:31,558
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the same image that popped up.

132
00:09:32,018 --> 00:09:34,038
[SPEAKER_01]: But one came through your own intention, one didn't.

133
00:09:35,058 --> 00:09:37,739
[SPEAKER_01]: If it's through your own intention, that's the center stage I talk about.

134
00:09:39,079 --> 00:09:43,220
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's actually... there's a whole universe of difference between the two.

135
00:09:44,141 --> 00:09:45,181
[SPEAKER_01]: But you need to arrive at it.

136
00:09:47,141 --> 00:09:48,502
[SPEAKER_01]: The difference is internal.

137
00:09:48,682 --> 00:09:50,142
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not in the content.

138
00:09:50,765 --> 00:09:51,505
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like that.

139
00:09:51,906 --> 00:09:55,787
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't know if I said it in some talk or just when we were speaking without recording.

140
00:09:55,807 --> 00:09:56,487
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like

141
00:10:21,642 --> 00:10:34,252
[SPEAKER_01]: You imagine you have like a, like a, like a, I don't know, a place with a glass in between, that is just like a, I don't know, a square meter of foot space, and there is like a transparent glass in between.

142
00:10:34,372 --> 00:10:35,753
[SPEAKER_01]: So it's like this on the same spot.

143
00:10:37,254 --> 00:10:45,461
[SPEAKER_01]: But the only way to get from one side of that glass, like 10 centimeters, well, not even 10, like one centimeter on the other side of the glass,

144
00:10:45,877 --> 00:10:51,120
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to go all the way around, completely, all the way around, to a different world, to arrive at the same thing.

145
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:54,542
[SPEAKER_01]: You still look at the same thing that's there, on that floor.

146
00:10:56,623 --> 00:10:58,564
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly it.

147
00:10:58,584 --> 00:11:00,766
[SPEAKER_01]: So you have the images and stuff that present themselves.

148
00:11:01,706 --> 00:11:08,210
[SPEAKER_01]: Untrained mind wouldn't see a difference between picking them up with your intention, and them coming up on their own.

149
00:11:09,430 --> 00:11:13,713
[SPEAKER_01]: And then it would think, I need to deal with the content, I need to deal with the thoughts themselves.

150
00:11:14,534 --> 00:11:18,196
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, no, you need to deal with your intention in thinking them.

151
00:11:19,417 --> 00:11:25,861
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's that practice of not allowing them the center stage while the blurry cloud is there waiting to crystallize.

152
00:11:25,901 --> 00:11:28,463
[SPEAKER_01]: But if it crystallizes on its own, you're free.

153
00:11:28,623 --> 00:11:29,964
[SPEAKER_01]: You're still free.

154
00:11:29,984 --> 00:11:30,905
[SPEAKER_01]: You're untouched by it.

155
00:11:31,905 --> 00:11:36,408
[SPEAKER_01]: If it crystallizes through your own intention of picking it up, that's what touches you.

156
00:11:39,370 --> 00:11:41,992
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the practice that can only be done indoors.

157
00:11:43,047 --> 00:11:48,109
[SPEAKER_01]: You can only do this practice and eventually discern this difference if the door remains closed.

158
00:11:49,329 --> 00:11:56,112
[SPEAKER_01]: If you go out to deal with stuff that's in front of your door, through your techniques and managements and stuff, none of this will be applicable.

159
00:11:56,352 --> 00:12:01,154
[SPEAKER_01]: This domain ceases to exist.

160
00:12:01,174 --> 00:12:02,515
[SPEAKER_01]: The distinction between those two?

161
00:12:02,755 --> 00:12:11,418
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, the distinction theoretically remains, but practical possibility of seeing it is gone.

162
00:12:12,227 --> 00:12:16,708
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you need to close the door for those distinctions to start to appear.

163
00:12:26,691 --> 00:12:27,051
[SPEAKER_01]: That's like...

164
00:12:27,071 --> 00:12:31,112
[SPEAKER_01]: So, imagine now... Say you're not... You're... You're...

165
00:12:31,372 --> 00:12:32,553
[SPEAKER_01]: There's a hindrance pressuring you.

166
00:12:32,573 --> 00:12:39,274
[SPEAKER_01]: Whether it's the doubt, ill-will, sensuality... You know the state of mind.

167
00:12:39,314 --> 00:12:41,435
[SPEAKER_01]: You know the general cloud that's waiting there.

168
00:12:42,109 --> 00:12:45,011
[SPEAKER_01]: Pressuring it to start intentionally crystallizing the thoughts.

169
00:12:47,172 --> 00:12:50,474
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you refrain... Again, I don't need to be cancelling the mind.

170
00:12:50,995 --> 00:12:56,679
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the painful part, when you think you need to be changing this weight and the direction of this weather.

171
00:12:57,459 --> 00:12:58,200
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's impossible.

172
00:12:58,400 --> 00:12:59,020
[SPEAKER_01]: But you don't actually...

173
00:12:59,040 --> 00:12:59,821
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't have to do that.

174
00:13:00,821 --> 00:13:06,545
[SPEAKER_01]: The sole reason that any of that would be a problem is if I'm making a connection, creating a connection,

175
00:13:07,370 --> 00:13:12,293
[SPEAKER_01]: Activation through intentionally crystallizing thoughts that are being pushed at me.

176
00:13:14,895 --> 00:13:21,539
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you are not allowing them the center stage... Say there is a mind that pressures you towards, I don't know, thoughts of ill will.

177
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:24,241
[SPEAKER_01]: Somebody knows you.

178
00:13:24,921 --> 00:13:29,584
[SPEAKER_01]: If you were to intentionally now go towards those thoughts, you know exactly what you will think.

179
00:13:29,804 --> 00:13:34,467
[SPEAKER_01]: But you're not doing that, so the pressure is there, but there is no specific thoughts of hatred that come from you.

180
00:13:35,842 --> 00:13:37,203
[SPEAKER_01]: What are you left with there and then?

181
00:13:38,304 --> 00:13:46,809
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, in your state, like, even imagine now, whatever subtle pressure you might be feeling on account of some hindrance, you're not allowing the center stage in regard to that very pressure.

182
00:13:47,389 --> 00:13:48,530
[SPEAKER_01]: What are you left with then, now?

183
00:13:50,851 --> 00:13:52,292
[SPEAKER_01]: The pressure.

184
00:13:53,193 --> 00:13:56,895
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, of course, the pressure is there, but broadly speaking...

185
00:13:56,915 --> 00:13:59,717
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, your body... Just basically here and now.

186
00:13:59,937 --> 00:14:00,137
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

187
